meta {
  name: Get Integration Inbound Queue Entity Definition
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

get {
  url: {{CRM_URL}}/EntityDefinitions(LogicalName='{{entityLogicalName}}')?$select=LogicalName,EntitySetName,PrimaryIdAttribute,PrimaryNameAttribute&$expand=Attributes($select=LogicalName,SchemaName,AttributeType,RequiredLevel,IsValidForCreate,IsValidForUpdate,DisplayName)
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  $select: LogicalName,EntitySetName,PrimaryIdAttribute,PrimaryNameAttribute
  $expand: Attributes($select=LogicalName,SchemaName,AttributeType,RequiredLevel,IsValidForCreate,IsValidForUpdate,DisplayName)
}

vars:pre-request {
  entityLogicalName: rpa_integrationinboundqueue
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: false
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Establishes the contract for the CRM integration inbound queue, the entity
  the doc-upload integration must write to when a submission cannot be turned
  into a correctly categorised case. Nothing in fcp-sfd-crm describes this
  entity, so its shape has to be read from Dataverse rather than assumed.

  Background: David Aitchison (DDTS CRM) confirmed on 9 July 2026 that a
  submission with unusable data must be reported as an error and stopped,
  never written to CRM with fallback values. The four conditions that must
  raise a record are an unresolvable CRN, an unresolvable SBI, no document
  type matching the case type, and a document type row found but missing
  scheme, subject, team routing or id.

  h4. Answer, from the rpadevv9 organisation

    LogicalName           rpa_integrationinboundqueue
    EntitySetName         rpa_integrationinboundqueues
    PrimaryIdAttribute    rpa_integrationinboundqueueid
    PrimaryNameAttribute  rpa_name

  The name used in the email, rpa_integrationinboundqueues, is the entity
  *set* name used in record URLs. EntityDefinitions is keyed on the logical
  name, the singular. Both are confirmed above.

  h4. Writable attributes

    rpa_name                  String    ApplicationRequired
    rpa_errordetails          Memo      optional
    rpa_xmlmessage            Memo      optional
    rpa_processingentity      Picklist  optional
    rpa_processingresult      Picklist  optional
    rpa_processingstage       Picklist  optional
    rpa_attempt               Integer   optional
    rpa_dateprocessed         DateTime  optional
    statuscode                Status    optional, valid for create
    rpa_integrationinboundqueueid  Uniqueidentifier, valid for create

  *rpa_name is the only attribute the write will fail without.* Everything
  else marked SystemRequired in the response is either a platform-managed
  virtual field or is not valid for create.

  Two consequences worth noting. The primary key is valid for create, so a
  deterministic GUID can be supplied and the record written create-only with
  If-None-Match: '*', which is how duplicate triage records are avoided on
  replay. And statecode is *not* valid for create, only for update, so the
  record's state is whatever the entity defaults to; only statuscode can be
  set at creation.

  h4. The gap this exposes

  *There is no attribute for CRN, SBI, case type or correlation identifier.*
  The entity has no field intended to carry them.

  rpa_errordetails is agreed with DDTS CRM as the field carrying the error
  details, and being a Memo it is not length constrained the way the string
  fields are. It is therefore also the only practical home for the
  correlation identifier, without which a triage record cannot be traced
  back to the message on the dead letter queue. Structure its content
  consistently rather than writing a free-text message, so a triager finds
  the identifier in the same place every time.

  MaxLength on rpa_name is not in the $select above, because it is exposed
  only on StringAttributeMetadata and selecting it here fails the whole
  request. Get it from "Get String Attribute MaxLength", changing the entity
  in that request's URL, before deciding what rpa_name carries.

  The three picklists and statuscode need their permitted values before
  anything can be written: see "Get Integration Inbound Queue Option Sets".

  h4. Per environment

  Run this against each environment before enabling the write there. The
  entity is solution-deployed, so its presence and shape in rpadevv9 proves
  neither in TEST, UAT nor PRODUCTION.
}
